compose/develop/.env
# `models` is a SYMLINK to the ext4 cache on this machine (scripts/link-models.ps1),
# not a directory in the repo. Ignore the entry itself, or git tracks a symlink
# pointing at a path that exists on exactly one machine.
/models
*.pyc
__pycache__/*
.env
# Backups of .env are still .env - the plain pattern above does not match a
# suffixed copy, so one made during a models move would be committed.
.env.bak*
*.env.bak*
!compose/develop/.env.example
# Core dumps. spconv-cu120 SIGFPEs on its first CUDA kernel here, and drops one
# into whatever directory it was launched from.
core.[0-9]*
.venv
compose/develop/db/data/
!images
images/*
# React build
frontend/node_modules/
src/sprite_generator/static/app/
# tsc -b writes this incremental cache on every build. It was tracked from the
# React port onward, so every front-end change left the tree dirty and four
# concurrent sessions kept re-committing each other's compile timestamps.
frontend/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
